Table full name: bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all
Column name: facility_place_id Type: STRING Description: The Google Place ID of the vaccination site. For example, ChIJV3woGFkSK4cRWP9s3-kIFGk.
Column name: facility_provider_id Type: STRING Description: An identifier imported from the provider of the vaccination site information. In the US, we use the ID provided by VaccineFinder when available. For example, 7ede5bd5-44da-4a59-b4d9-b3a49c53472c.
Column name: facility_name Type: STRING Description: The name of the vaccination site. For example, St. Joseph's Hospital.
Column name: facility_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: The latitude of the vaccination site. For example, 36.0507
Column name: facility_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: The longitude of the vaccination site. For example, 41.4356
Column name: facility_country_region Type: STRING Description: The name of the country or region in English. For example, United States.
Column name: facility_country_region_code Type: STRING Description: The ISO 3166-1 code for the country or region. For example, US.
Column name: facility_sub_region_1 Type: STRING Description: The name of a region in the country. For example, California.
Column name: facility_sub_region_1_code Type: STRING Description: A country-specific ISO 3166-2 code for the region. For example, US-CA.
Column name: facility_sub_region_2 Type: STRING Description: The name (or type) of a region in the country. Typically a subdivision of sub_region_1. For example, Santa Clara County or municipal_borough.
Column name: facility_sub_region_2_code Type: STRING Description: In the US, the FIPS code for a US county (or equivalent). For example, 06085.
Column name: facility_region_place_id Type: STRING Description: The Google place ID for the most-specific region, used in Google Places API and on Google Maps. For example, ChIJd_Y0eVIvkIARuQyDN0F1LBA.
Column name: mode_of_transportation Type: STRING Description: The mode of transport used to calculate the catchment boundary. For example, driving.
Column name: travel_time_threshold_minutes Type: INT64 Description: The maximum travel time, in minutes, used to calculate the catchment boundary. For example, 30.
Column name: facility_catchment_boundary Type: GEOGRAPHY Description: A GeoJSON representation of the catchment area boundary of the site, for a particular mode of transportation and travel time threshold. Consists of multiple latitude and longitude points.
