Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr  
• geo_id : 5‑digit county FIPS code – join key to vaccination table  
• do_date : the reference date for each ACS release – used for “latest” record per county  
• total_pop : total population – denominator for “sites per 1 000 people”  

bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all  
• facility_place_id : unique vaccination‑site identifier – used to count sites  
• facility_sub_region_1 : state name – filter to ‘California’  
• facility_sub_region_2_code : 5‑digit county FIPS – join key to ACS  
• facility_country_region_code : ISO‑country code – keep only ‘US’ records  

Typical conditions that will be applied  
• SUBSTR(geo_id,1,2)=‘06’  (California’s state FIPS)  
• facility_country_region_code='US'  
• facility_sub_region_1='California'  
• Get the row with max(do_date) per county to obtain “latest” population  

